1
00:00:01,290 --> 00:00:04,290
Man, Japan is ridiculously hot.

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:05,920
Yeah, it is.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,560
How's Toda doing?

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,760
Huh?

5
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:13,880
No, I mean his leg injury.

6
00:00:14,010 --> 00:00:16,510
Oh... It seems like it's nothing serious.

7
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:17,920
Yeah.

8
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:19,540
That's good.

9
00:00:19,970 --> 00:00:21,660
Oh, if you see Toda,

10
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:24,490
tell him I want to show him
the video from the island.

11
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,100
Sure.

12
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,730
I'd like to hear his thoughts on it, too.

13
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:39,340
You know what,

14
00:00:39,450 --> 00:00:40,970
I think I'll just contact him myself.

15
00:00:41,950 --> 00:00:43,810
I'm heading to the film club now.

16
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:44,870
See ya.

17
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:56,530
But... I just can't help but think
about what happened back then.

18
00:01:04,460 --> 00:01:05,490
I'm sorry...

19
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:45,600
"My Summer Of You"
(Episode 12)

20
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,540
Oh, Niimi-san.

21
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:50,140
Oh, Saeki-kun?

22
00:02:50,790 --> 00:02:52,190
Thanks for your help the other day.

23
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:54,380
I should be the one
thanking you for everything.

24
00:02:55,340 --> 00:02:56,780
You're here looking for Toda, right?

25
00:02:56,960 --> 00:02:57,960
Yes.

26
00:02:58,010 --> 00:02:59,510
I was wondering if he was around.

27
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,850
He has the day off today.

28
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,410
Oh, do you want me to contact him for you?

29
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:15,020
No, it's fine.

30
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:17,690
Sorry for interrupting your work.

31
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,390
I'll be going now.

32
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:21,270
Ah, wait a sec.

33
00:03:22,360 --> 00:03:23,720
Do you have some time right now?

34
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:30,161
(Wataru: It's fine, just a sprain.)

35
00:03:30,186 --> 00:03:31,999
(Chiharu: I'm really sorry for hiding
the study abroad thing from you.)

36
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,539
(Chiharu: If you can still forgive me, I'd
like to see you again and talk things out.)

37
00:03:50,180 --> 00:03:51,190
Hello?

38
00:03:56,610 --> 00:03:58,360
Well, how should I put this?

39
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:03,170
Beating around the bush is
weird, so I'll just ask you straight.

40
00:04:03,280 --> 00:04:04,720
Are you and Toda dating?

41
00:04:05,030 --> 00:04:06,030
Huh...

42
00:04:07,240 --> 00:04:08,240
Ah...

43
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:12,080
I guess it's a bit unfair to ask like that.

44
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:15,270
No, the truth is,

45
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:20,480
I forgot to return Toda's phone on the day
of the dinner, so I went back to the park.

46
00:04:21,510 --> 00:04:22,510
What?

47
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:26,990
I didn't mean to spy, but...

48
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:35,560
I had a feeling that might be
the case, so I thought I'd ask.

49
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,190
No, we're the ones who should apologize.

50
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:43,900
I see.

51
00:04:47,530 --> 00:04:49,330
You're not surprised.

52
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,700
Huh?

53
00:04:51,330 --> 00:04:52,330
Ah...

54
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:54,290
It's nothing out of the ordinary.

55
00:04:54,670 --> 00:04:56,190
After all, I used to be like that too.

56
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:57,960
What?

57
00:04:58,730 --> 00:05:02,770
Though I've only dated
someone of the same sex once.

58
00:05:03,090 --> 00:05:05,800
It's just that we broke up
over a huge misunderstanding.

59
00:05:06,470 --> 00:05:09,140
That's why I'm particularly
invested in you two.

60
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:21,430
Was Toda's strong reaction to
Blueprint on the island related to this?

61
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:27,780
In the past... I did
something really stupid.

62
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:30,370
Something stupid?

63
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,980
I think you should really see this, Toda.

64
00:06:27,930 --> 00:06:29,030
What do you think?

65
00:06:30,150 --> 00:06:31,320
What do you mean...

66
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,060
No...

67
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:37,540
Even though I don't know what
exactly happened between you two,

68
00:06:37,670 --> 00:06:40,690
I feel like Chiharu

69
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,540
really cares about you, Toda.

70
00:06:44,650 --> 00:06:45,650
Huh...

71
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:49,190
Regarding his thoughts on Blueprint,

72
00:06:50,240 --> 00:06:51,950
what do you think Chiharu said?

73
00:07:01,190 --> 00:07:05,650
"I want to cherish the time I spend
with the person who matters most to me."

74
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:11,150
That's what he said.

75
00:07:22,810 --> 00:07:25,420
So, are you regretting it now?

76
00:07:26,710 --> 00:07:29,800
Even if I regret it, all of
this is very important to me.

77
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:35,870
I actually regret it quite a bit.

78
00:07:37,090 --> 00:07:39,910
If we had just communicated
our feelings properly back then,

79
00:07:40,540 --> 00:07:42,470
could we have overcome that hurdle?

80
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,840
Niimi-san, I'm sorry.

81
00:07:48,960 --> 00:07:51,530
Something came up. Please excuse me.

82
00:08:14,030 --> 00:08:15,490
You're not going to answer?

83
00:08:16,310 --> 00:08:17,310
Hello?

84
00:08:18,660 --> 00:08:20,620
Wataru, where are you right now?

85
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:22,080
Huh?

86
00:08:22,670 --> 00:08:25,640
I know it's sudden, but
can we meet up right now?

87
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,750
There's something I
really need to tell you.

88
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,560
I'll come to you, no matter where you are.

89
00:08:31,770 --> 00:08:32,770
Sorry, I...

90
00:08:33,090 --> 00:08:37,799
Platform 1. The train bound for
Moriya Beach is about to depart...

91
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:39,700
Sorry, I'm in a hurry.

92
00:08:43,390 --> 00:08:44,390
Wataru...

93
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:13,480
He's been like this
from the very beginning.

94
00:09:14,970 --> 00:09:19,780
Even when he confessed to me, he
was always worrying about my feelings.

95
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,770
It's another hour until the next bus.

96
00:09:33,110 --> 00:09:35,550
Thinking alone, suffering alone.

97
00:09:37,410 --> 00:09:39,680
And then disappearing right in front of me.

98
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:49,500
Even though I already forgave him once,

99
00:10:03,750 --> 00:10:07,270
I'm still stuck in that summer.

100
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:43,280
Wataru.

101
00:10:47,310 --> 00:10:48,810
Sorry I'm late.

102
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:52,830
Whatever.

103
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,320
It's not like I asked you to come.

104
00:10:57,950 --> 00:10:59,070
That's true.

105
00:11:03,450 --> 00:11:04,740
Have a seat.

106
00:11:07,250 --> 00:11:08,250
Yeah.

107
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,010
What were you just doing?

108
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:33,540
Thinking about that summer.

109
00:11:38,780 --> 00:11:41,150
I told you before that
you haven't changed at all.

110
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:45,410
But I'm exactly the same as I was in
high school. I haven't changed either.

111
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,260
Thinking about it now still pisses me off.

112
00:11:48,910 --> 00:11:50,040
And it hurts, too.

113
00:11:54,890 --> 00:11:56,250
But I still wanted to see you.

114
00:11:59,800 --> 00:12:02,090
My mind is a total mess.

115
00:12:03,680 --> 00:12:04,800
Wataru...

116
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:13,370
I'm still stuck in that summer.

117
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:21,070
That's all my fault.

118
00:12:22,900 --> 00:12:25,800
I'm the one who dragged
you back to that summer.

119
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:34,959
If I had told you about studying abroad,

120
00:12:34,960 --> 00:12:37,250
I know you would have supported me.

121
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:42,270
But I was terrified that
it would hurt you again.

122
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:45,300
I was afraid of losing you.

123
00:12:48,930 --> 00:12:50,850
In the end, I still...

124
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,910
If you hadn't chased after me back then,

125
00:13:08,160 --> 00:13:10,090
we wouldn't be where we are today.

126
00:13:12,290 --> 00:13:14,770
So this time, it's my
turn to chase after you.

127
00:13:18,170 --> 00:13:20,250
Until you can trust me again.

128
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:25,550
I want to face everything
about you, Wataru.

129
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:36,060
I won't leave your side.

130
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:40,080
That's my resolve now.

131
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:52,550
Even though that should be a given...

132
00:14:07,760 --> 00:14:09,570
Wataru, what's wrong?

133
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:13,120
What do you mean, what's wrong?

134
00:14:14,520 --> 00:14:15,890
You're crying.

135
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:18,140
Huh...

136
00:14:22,270 --> 00:14:23,610
What the hell is this?

137
00:14:24,110 --> 00:14:26,590
No, I didn't mean to cry at all.

138
00:14:30,030 --> 00:14:32,430
Seriously, what the hell?

139
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:34,930
The tears just won't stop.

140
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:38,620
Seriously...

141
00:14:39,500 --> 00:14:42,170
I was planning to beat the crap out of you.

142
00:14:50,550 --> 00:14:51,680
I'm sorry.

143
00:14:51,970 --> 00:14:53,140
For hurting you.

144
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:01,830
I was so scared.

145
00:15:04,150 --> 00:15:05,860
I was really frustrated.

146
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,450
It hurt so much.

147
00:15:11,990 --> 00:15:13,240
And I was so sad.

148
00:15:18,210 --> 00:15:19,500
I'm sorry, Wataru.

149
00:15:21,830 --> 00:15:23,500
I'm so, so sorry.

150
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:57,800
Um,

151
00:15:58,410 --> 00:16:00,010
I'll ask you one more time.

152
00:16:00,370 --> 00:16:01,570
Are you really okay with this?

153
00:16:03,670 --> 00:16:05,090
Stop asking me so many times.

154
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:10,270
Because you're so kind, Wataru.

155
00:16:12,050 --> 00:16:14,900
You always want to give me
whatever I hope for, don't you?

156
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:21,480
Knowing that and still doing it makes
me feel like I'm taking advantage of you.

157
00:16:23,020 --> 00:16:24,610
It feels unfair.

158
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,320
Seriously.

159
00:16:30,100 --> 00:16:31,260
You idiot.

160
00:16:32,650 --> 00:16:34,200
That's exactly what I mean about you.

161
00:16:34,950 --> 00:16:37,430
Always making assumptions on
your own and overthinking things.

162
00:16:39,580 --> 00:16:41,430
Did I ever say I hated it?

163
00:16:44,340 --> 00:16:45,380
No.

164
00:16:47,960 --> 00:16:50,020
Since you've made up your mind,

165
00:16:51,590 --> 00:16:53,220
I want to make up my mind, too.

166
00:16:58,890 --> 00:16:59,770
What?

167
00:16:59,850 --> 00:17:01,020
Sorry, sorry.

168
00:17:16,600 --> 00:17:17,700
I love you so much.

169
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:18,980
Wataru.

170
00:17:22,620 --> 00:17:23,620
Me too.

171
00:17:58,700 --> 00:18:00,260
Morning, Wataru.

172
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:08,540
Morning.

173
00:18:08,710 --> 00:18:09,710
Chiharu.

174
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:24,930
I feel like this is the
closest I've ever felt to you.

175
00:18:33,530 --> 00:18:35,439
Stop it! Oh crap!

176
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:37,349
What was that sound?

177
00:18:37,350 --> 00:18:38,709
It's your fault.

178
00:18:38,710 --> 00:18:40,150
Stop messing around.

179
00:18:40,240 --> 00:18:41,369
I'm gonna fight back.

180
00:18:41,370 --> 00:18:42,870
Stop it, stop!

181
00:18:43,290 --> 00:18:44,290
You jerk.

182
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:46,940
Okay.

183
00:18:47,230 --> 00:18:48,500
- Please come in.
- Thank you.

184
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:53,550
Hey, we're here to see the movie.

185
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:54,880
Guchi, Hiraoka.

186
00:18:54,920 --> 00:18:56,550
You look like a real staff member.

187
00:18:56,590 --> 00:18:57,590
Right?

188
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:02,260
Is that the legendary
glasses senpai over there?

189
00:19:02,570 --> 00:19:03,570
Ah, yeah, yeah.

190
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:05,810
That's Niimi-san.

191
00:19:09,270 --> 00:19:11,870
I feel an intense stare
coming from over there.

192
00:19:12,530 --> 00:19:15,150
There's a cute kid looking at you.

193
00:19:17,990 --> 00:19:18,990
What!?

194
00:19:24,450 --> 00:19:25,450
I win.

195
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:26,579
How did you win?

196
00:19:26,580 --> 00:19:27,580
Uh.

197
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:28,709
Why is Asada here?

198
00:19:28,710 --> 00:19:29,920
What do you mean, "uh"?

199
00:19:30,070 --> 00:19:31,470
Can't I come see a movie by myself?

200
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:33,840
It was an "Uh, how have
you been?" kind of "uh."

201
00:19:34,090 --> 00:19:36,810
Wataru, wanna go to karaoke
after work? It's been a while.

202
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:37,810
Karaoke?

203
00:19:37,811 --> 00:19:39,409
- I'm down!
- Huh?

204
00:19:39,410 --> 00:19:41,430
Sorry, I have plans.

205
00:19:41,590 --> 00:19:42,590
What?

206
00:19:42,710 --> 00:19:44,169
Wataru, don't tell me you're...

207
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:45,719
Don't bother him while he's working.

208
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:46,470
Hold on.

209
00:19:46,471 --> 00:19:47,609
Wataru, let's go to
karaoke together next time.

210
00:19:47,610 --> 00:19:48,770
Sure, see you next time.

211
00:19:51,610 --> 00:19:55,230
Where's the timeline
where I get to be Toda?

212
00:19:55,690 --> 00:19:57,480
Maybe in your next life.

213
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,610
I'd rather have it in this one.

214
00:20:04,090 --> 00:20:07,490
Wow, the big screen really packs a punch.

215
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:09,780
It's nice to go to a different
theater once in a while.

216
00:20:09,870 --> 00:20:10,870
Yeah, it is.

217
00:20:11,730 --> 00:20:12,730
By the way,

218
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,880
There's something I need to tell you.

219
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:16,750
What is it?

220
00:20:17,290 --> 00:20:20,480
I actually ran into
Niimi-san the other day.

221
00:20:22,760 --> 00:20:27,260
What? He saw us?
Are you serious?

222
00:20:27,310 --> 00:20:29,390
There was no hiding it in that situation.

223
00:20:29,430 --> 00:20:32,520
It's your fault for doing that outside.

224
00:20:33,650 --> 00:20:35,360
You were the one who started it.

225
00:20:37,410 --> 00:20:38,410
Huh?

226
00:20:39,390 --> 00:20:41,990
You really don't remember, do you?

227
00:20:44,270 --> 00:20:45,320
No way.

228
00:20:47,450 --> 00:20:49,120
Sorry.

229
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:56,340
It's fine. I just...

230
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:01,300
What?

231
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:07,640
I was just wondering how I
ended up liking you so much.

232
00:21:08,510 --> 00:21:11,930
I love you so much, Wataru,
it even surprises me.

233
00:21:12,870 --> 00:21:14,020
That makes me really happy.

234
00:21:17,570 --> 00:21:20,980
I can feel that.

235
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,240
Why are you being so formal?

236
00:21:26,570 --> 00:21:27,570
You know,

237
00:21:27,730 --> 00:21:29,699
Since you're always saying
how much you like me,

238
00:21:29,700 --> 00:21:30,700
I kind of feel like...

239
00:21:32,330 --> 00:21:33,460
Feel like what?

240
00:21:34,790 --> 00:21:38,350
Even though I really like you too,
I feel like I'm being outdone.

241
00:21:39,880 --> 00:21:43,190
Then I want you to kiss me first.

242
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:44,720
Huh?

243
00:21:55,770 --> 00:21:57,530
I guess you can't do
it unless you're drunk?

244
00:21:59,650 --> 00:22:00,650
I can.

245
00:22:02,210 --> 00:22:03,210
Huh?

246
00:22:04,670 --> 00:22:07,610
If you close your eyes...

247
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:46,700
Hey, come on.

248
00:22:49,490 --> 00:22:52,620
Wataru, thank you for trying so hard.

249
00:22:57,580 --> 00:22:58,580
Huh?

250
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:04,550
Can we hold hands for a bit?

251
00:23:05,090 --> 00:23:06,130
Hold on a second.

252
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:14,850
I...

253
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:16,260
I'm going to work really hard.

254
00:23:17,680 --> 00:23:22,060
Hard enough so that I never let go
of this hand you're holding, Wataru.

255
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:44,040
Yeah.

256
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:45,880
Do your best.

257
00:23:46,570 --> 00:23:47,570
Chiharu.

258
00:23:50,670 --> 00:23:54,010
The season that makes me
want to cry is always summer.

259
00:23:59,890 --> 00:24:01,980
Wataru, I love you.

260
00:24:05,730 --> 00:24:07,860
I've loved you ever since then.

261
00:24:10,570 --> 00:24:12,490
That's been quite a few years.

262
00:24:14,370 --> 00:24:16,120
Ever since that day,

263
00:24:17,950 --> 00:24:19,790
you've always been in the midst of summer.

264
00:24:23,380 --> 00:24:25,170
From now on, autumn will come,

265
00:24:25,610 --> 00:24:26,880
winter will come,

266
00:24:28,490 --> 00:24:29,670
spring will come,

267
00:24:29,850 --> 00:24:31,630
and even when summer comes around again,

268
00:24:41,270 --> 00:24:42,830
I will still love you.
